/target

# Harness runtime state, when the binary is run from this directory rather
# than from the container's working directory.
#
# `main.rs` opens `<root>/session.jsonl` on every run, and the interp seam
# writes `probe-flags.jsonl` beside it. In the container that root is
# `/sessions`, which the repository .gitignore already covers; a `cargo run`
# or a profiling run started here puts them in the worktree instead, where
# they show up as untracked files that look like something worth committing
# and are not. They are per-run state: a transcript of one conversation.
#
# Not a test artifact. The tests write into `tempfile::tempdir()` and clean up
# after themselves; this is only ever the real binary having been run.
/session.jsonl
/probe-flags.jsonl
